      "text": [
        ": سَأَلْتُ أَبَا عَبْدِ اَللَّهِ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ عَنْ رَجُلٍ شَجَّ رَجُلاً مُوضِحَةً وَ شَجَّهُ آخَرُ دَامِيَةً فِي مَقَامٍ وَاحِدٍ فَمَاتَ اَلرَّجُلُ قَالَ \"عَلَيْهِمَا اَلدِّيَةُ فِي أَمْوَالِهِمَا نِصْفَيْنِ\"."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.5383 - Al-Hasan ibn Mahbub narrated from Salih ibn Razin, from Dharih Al-Muharibi, who said: I asked Abu Abdullah (as) about a man who was struck by one person with a muḍihah wound (a wound that exposes the bone) and by another person with a damiyah wound (a bleeding wound) in the same instance, and the man died.\nImam (as) said: \"The blood money is upon both of them, divided equally between their wealth.\""
        ]
      }
